12... { -KEY- } Ng6 { Often the best placement for the knight in the Berlin endgame. The knight avoids obstructing the light-squared bishop, and at the same time makes it harder for White to prepare Nd4 and f2-f4 (as the e5-pawn would be hanging). Black will continue developing with ...Bb4 or ...Be7, and will then prepare to exchange a pair of rooks with ...Rd8. } ( 12... Be6 13. Nd4 $16 ) 
 ( { A test solver noted } 12... a5 13. a3 Ng6 14. Nd4 Nxe5 15. Bf4 Nc4 16. Ndb5 $16 { as an argument for not starting with 12...a5. A better argument is that we should develop pieces before pawns, unless there's a truly compelling reason not to. } ) 

